# Project-file body inference

Cold project indexing must run TypeTracker, higher-order calls, local flow, and inferred method returns for **every project file**.

Do not:

- Defer that walk to `didOpen` / open buffers only
- Infer only methods referenced from the current file
- Publish `Unknown` to mean "this closed file was not inferred yet"

`Unknown` means the proof was attempted and failed. Declared returns (RBS, YARD, constructors) are separate from inferred body returns.

Indexing latency comes from cheapening the visitor, not skipping it. Unchanged `didOpen` reuses cold-index facts. Body-only `didChange` still stays on the current file.

Canonical write-up: `AGENTS.md` (Type Inference Architecture + Performance Backlog) and `crates/ruby-analysis/src/inference/mod.rs`.
